    2  A   ablation_onset           2.250    79.12   4.081e+04  stylized
          Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on
          (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's
          light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~79 km as low-confidence.
          Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin,
          volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
    3  Y   first_yield              4.458    58.67   1.302e+06  physical
          Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.07 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and
          heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5
          / H_f in [R22]).
    4  -   drag_overtakes_ablation   4.460    58.65   1.306e+06  stylized
          Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio
          ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14
          km/s (from the model's heating law).
    5  F   flare                    4.482    58.46   3.041e+06  stylized
          Light rises x4.7 in 0.13 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with:
          yield gen 0 at 58.6 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 58.2 km (99% of m0). Dust groups supply
          34% of the rise and 27% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare
          (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic
          cascade.
    6  B   first_breakup            4.502    58.26   5.663e+06  stylized
